# trail-of-signs — pattern
@id trail-of-signs  @kind pattern  @layer library  @author toine  @lang en

## summary
~ A line of marks leads somewhere. The carrier reads them better than the player (trade, habit, kinship), so the player depends on her eyes; the last sign asks to leave the obvious way.

## roles
role reader : character : who can read the signs
role sign* : thing : one mark in the line (attrs: fact, line)
role leave_fact : fact : the sign that says "leave the obvious way"
role destination : station : where the signs lead

## facts_required
need code : fact : what the signs mean, once read

## principles
! $reader reads every sign she is shown, in her own trade words.
~0.7 A sign misread by the player is corrected by the reader, kindly or not.

## rules
when look.at($sign) once -> reveal($sign.fact), say($sign.line) {sign-read}

## beats_hint
hint first sign early and easy; the second needs the reader's trade
hint the last sign stands at a fork

## variations
variation false-trail : one sign was made by someone else; the reader notices the difference in hand
